// ============================================================
// 🔥 ACHIEVING ACID VIA SERIAL EXECUTION (COMPLETE NOTES)
// ============================================================


// ============================================================
// 🧠 0. BACKGROUND: PROBLEM KYA THA?
// ============================================================

// Humne dekha:
// - Write Skew ❌
// - Phantom Writes ❌

// Root cause:
// Concurrent transactions ek hi data ko dekh ke decisions lete hain
// → conflict invisible ho jata hai
// → incorrect final state

// 👉 Core problem:
// "Concurrency = Bugs (if not handled properly)"


// ============================================================
// 💡 BIG IDEA:
// ============================================================

// Agar concurrency problem hai...
// 👉 TOH CONCURRENCY HATA DO 😎

// Means:
// 👉 Transactions ko sequential chalao

// 👉 Isko bolte hain: SERIAL EXECUTION


// ============================================================
// 🔥 1. ACTUAL SERIAL EXECUTION
// ============================================================

// 🧠 Definition:
// Transactions run one after another (NO overlap)


// ============================================================
// ⚙️ EXECUTION FLOW
// ============================================================

// Instead of:
// T1 --------
//     T2 --------

// We do:
// T1 --------
//             T2 --------
//                         T3 --------


// ============================================================
// 🏠 REAL LIFE ANALOGY
// ============================================================

// ATM Machine 🏧

// Ek time pe sirf ek banda use karta hai:
// - Banda 1 kaam karega
// - Complete hone ke baad Banda 2 aayega

// 👉 Isliye:
// - No double withdrawal
// - No race condition
// - Always correct result


// ============================================================
// ✅ WHAT PROBLEMS DOES IT SOLVE?
// ============================================================

// ✔ Write Skew → impossible
// ✔ Phantom Writes → impossible
// ✔ Dirty Reads → impossible
// ✔ Lost Updates → impossible

// 👉 FULL ACID GUARANTEE


// ============================================================
// 🧠 WHY IT WORKS?
// ============================================================

// Kyunki:
// - Koi 2 transactions ek saath run nahi kar rahe
// - Har transaction latest committed data dekhta hai

// 👉 No stale reads
// 👉 No race condition


// ============================================================
// ❌ PROBLEMS WITH SERIAL EXECUTION
// ============================================================

// 🚨 1. PERFORMANCE ISSUE

// Imagine:
// 10,000 users → sab line me wait kar rahe 😭

// Throughput ↓↓↓


// ------------------------------------------------------------

// 🚨 2. CPU UNDERUTILIZATION

// Modern systems multi-core hote hain
// But yahan:
// → sirf 1 transaction run ho raha hai

// 👉 Baaki resources idle


// ------------------------------------------------------------

// 🚨 3. LONG TRANSACTIONS = SYSTEM BLOCK

// Example:

// T1:
// - Read data
// - Call external API (slow)
// - Write data

// 👉 Jab tak T1 finish nahi karega:
// T2, T3, T4 → WAITING 😭


// ------------------------------------------------------------

// 🚨 4. NOT SCALABLE

// High traffic systems (Amazon, UPI, etc)
// me ye approach fail ho jaata hai


// ------------------------------------------------------------

// 🚨 5. SINGLE PIPELINE BOTTLENECK

// Sirf ek execution path
// → system choke ho jata hai


// ============================================================
// 🔥 LIMITS SUMMARY
// ============================================================

// Serial Execution:
// ✔ Correctness = 100%
// ❌ Performance = very poor

// 👉 Tradeoff:
// Correctness vs Performance


// ============================================================
// 💡 ENGINEERING CHALLENGE
// ============================================================

// Question:
// "Kaise correctness maintain karein,
// but performance bhi improve karein?"


// ============================================================
// 🚀 2. STORED PROCEDURES (OPTIMIZATION)
// ============================================================

// 🧠 Definition:
// Stored Procedure = DB ke andar stored function
// jo ek hi call me poora transaction execute karta hai


// ============================================================
// 🏠 REAL LIFE ANALOGY
// ============================================================

// Restaurant 🍽️

// ❌ Without Stored Procedure:
// - Order do
// - Waiter kitchen jaata hai
// - Wapas aata hai
// - Phir next instruction

// 👉 Multiple trips → slow


// ------------------------------------------------------------

// ✅ With Stored Procedure:

// Chef ko bol diya:
// "Bhai pura combo bana de"

// 👉 Ek hi baar me sab ready

// 👉 Fast execution


// ============================================================
// ⚙️ TECHNICAL EXAMPLE
// ============================================================

// ❌ Without Stored Procedure:

// Step 1:
SELECT balance FROM account WHERE id = 1;

// Step 2:
UPDATE account SET balance = balance - 100 WHERE id = 1;

// Step 3:
UPDATE account SET balance = balance + 100 WHERE id = 2;

// 👉 Multiple network round trips


// ------------------------------------------------------------

// ✅ With Stored Procedure:

/*
CREATE PROCEDURE transfer_money()
BEGIN
    UPDATE account SET balance = balance - 100 WHERE id = 1;
    UPDATE account SET balance = balance + 100 WHERE id = 2;
END;
*/

// 👉 Single call → full execution


// ============================================================
// 🧠 WHY STORED PROCEDURES HELP?
// ============================================================

// Goal:
// Transaction duration kam karna

// Before:
// Transaction time = LONG
// → system blocked longer

// After:
// Transaction time = SHORT
// → faster queue movement


// ============================================================
// ✅ ADVANTAGES
// ============================================================

// 🚀 1. FAST EXECUTION
// - No network latency
// - Everything inside DB


// ------------------------------------------------------------

// 🚀 2. HIGHER THROUGHPUT
// - Transactions jaldi complete
// - More transactions per second


// ------------------------------------------------------------

// 🚀 3. BETTER FOR SERIAL EXECUTION
// - Short transactions → less blocking


// ------------------------------------------------------------

// 🚀 4. REDUCED CLIENT LOGIC
// - Business logic DB handle karta hai


// ============================================================
// ❌ DISADVANTAGES
// ============================================================

// 🚨 1. HARD TO DEBUG
// - DB ke andar code
// - Debugging tools limited


// ------------------------------------------------------------

// 🚨 2. VENDOR LOCK-IN
// - MySQL vs PostgreSQL vs Oracle syntax different


// ------------------------------------------------------------

// 🚨 3. LIMITED FLEXIBILITY
// - Complex logic likhna mushkil


// ------------------------------------------------------------

// 🚨 4. DB OVERLOAD RISK
// - Zyada logic DB pe shift ho jata hai


// ============================================================
// 🔥 BIG PICTURE (EVOLUTION)
// ============================================================

// STEP 1:
// Concurrent Execution
// → Fast but incorrect ❌


// ------------------------------------------------------------

// STEP 2:
// Serial Execution
// → Correct but slow ❌


// ------------------------------------------------------------

// STEP 3:
// Serial + Stored Procedures
// → Correct + Faster ✅


// ============================================================
// 🧠 CORE INSIGHT (VERY IMPORTANT)
// ============================================================

// 👉 "Remove concurrency → remove anomalies"

// BUT:
// 👉 "Removing concurrency → kills performance"

// So:
// 👉 Optimize execution time (Stored Procedures)


// ============================================================
// 🔥 INTERVIEW READY ANSWER
// ============================================================

// Q: How can databases achieve ACID?

// Answer:
// "One approach is serial execution, where transactions are run
// sequentially to eliminate concurrency anomalies like write skew
// and phantom writes. However, this reduces performance.
// To mitigate this, stored procedures are used to reduce
// transaction duration and improve throughput while maintaining correctness."


